Modern WordPress plugin featuring an MVC structure, dependency injection container, Composer autoloading, Docker support, and Webpack build pipeline.

## Folder structure

All php files reside in `inc`. All `psr-4` classes will be autoloaded via `composer` from the `app` folder.

All raw js, css, and blocks reside in `src`. These are files that need to be built during the build process.

## Installation

Clone or download this repository.

```bash
npm install

composer install

composer dump-autoload

```

## Usage

### Docker

Docker set up to control the development environment. You must have `docker` and `docker-compose` installed.

Docker env variables for php and wordpress versions will be set in `.env`. The wordpress `debug.log` file from the docker container will be placed in the projects root directory.

### Dev Scripts

```bash
npm run build

```

Development run.

```bash
docker compose up -d

npm run dev

```

To archive your plugin for distribution run.

```bash
npm run archive:plugin

```

To archive your entire development version of the plugin. This can be handy if your developing for a client and need to ship the entire plugin contents.

```bash
npm run archive:dev

```

## Blocks

### Create a block

Use the `create:block` npm script supplied. Block information can be controlled in the `config.json` file. Any additional `block.json` defaults may be placed here in the `json` field.

Then just run the command below specifying the block type `dynamic` or `static` and changing `my-block` to your desired block slug:

( Note: the slug should be dash seperated. Eg. `my-block` )

```bash
npm run create:block dynamic my-block

```

The script will create your block files in `src/blocks`. Block files will use typescript by default. Edit the `block.json` file to your liking. The `create:block` script uses basically the same templates wordpress does `https://github.com/WordPress/gutenberg/tree/trunk/packages/create-block/lib/templates/block`. They have been modified slightly for use with typescript.

### Register a block

Once you have successfully created a block all you have to do is add the block slug to the `register` array in `inc/config/block-config.php`. This array assumes your blocks source files are located in the `src/blocks` folder and built to `build/blocks` folder.
